st all 17
2026-09-04T08:39Z claude note SESSION STOPPED at 96% of the week's usage budget, export still not produced. Three further findings from actually running it, in order. (1) The 57-minute inject run earlier almost exactly matched reindex_fulltext's hardcoded max_wait=3600 (1 hour) -- items were created (write_items happens before the reindex-wait) but the function itself likely never returned cleanly; nobody had checked its exit status, only that items existed. FIXED: reindex_fulltext required state=="indexed" for every key, so any recipe containing a document with no extractable text (DjVu, an un-OCR'd scan) could never complete -- it would always burn the full hour then raise. Rewritten to accept any real settled state (idle -- not busy, not running -- held across two consecutive polls, not a momentary gap between queuing and starting) rather than demanding "indexed" specifically; an item Zotero genuinely finished trying and left unindexed is real ground truth for a failure-control fixture, not a reason to hang. Tested (test_reindex_accepts_a_genuinely_settled_unindexed_state, test_reindex_still_times_out_when_genuinely_never_idle, test_reindex_idle_must_hold_across_two_polls_not_one); full suite green; this fix is committed, real progress independent of the rest. (2) Re-running export with the fix took about a minute instead of an hour, but failed on a THIRD undoable document not previously known: ramsey-1931-foundations-of-mathematics (K6VK5Y68) -- confirmed directly (pdftotext, pdffonts against the live cached file): 340 pages, 340 bytes of extracted text, zero embedded fonts, same profile as the Vietnamese no-OCR scan. Not a bug, a genuine third failure-control case; the author's same-session ruling on the Vietnamese pair plainly extends here but has not been asked or stated by name for this document specifically. (3) _snapshot_rows hard-requires every attachment to appear in the /fulltext census (raises "no /fulltext census entry" otherwise); census only lists i