--- body ---
## Context

Ticket 0029's tracker (its "## Children" table, and the "Sequencing is
unchanged" paragraph above it) names this as the first child to file: "the
harness triplet (injection script, export snapshot, Zotero-free replay),
against the 17 already-hashed documents" — unblocked, since it does not wait
on the 9 records still stuck behind browser-only challenge pages (4 HAL,
4 Gallica, 1 Malynes).

Most of the harness code already exists, built before the tracker/child-ticket
convention landed on 0029. It shipped in PR #294 ("0029: build the golden
fixture injection and offline replay harness", merged 2026-09-03,
`54525bb`), not PR #298 as an earlier note on this work mistakenly said —
`gh pr view 298` is a stranded-branch recovery PR unrelated to this code;
`f84b523` and its follow-ups (`b2cc16e`, `9c1823a`, `0305116`, `c47555d`,
`a8bfcb6`, then the `/gaze` simplify pass `c04674f`) are the real history and
all land inside #294. That PR's own body says plainly what it does not do:
"This does not close 0029. The nine remaining source hashes, live public-
library injection/export, reviewed query and answer set, passage distribution,
and 0581 gate wiring remain open."

So what is actually still missing, verified directly rather than assumed
(rules/workflow.md § Diagnosis discipline): a *real* injection + export has
never been run. `bench/fixtures/golden_fixture.py inject`/`export` need a
public Zotero library to write into — `--library-type` defaults to `group`
and `--library-id` is required; there is no default and no fallback to the
personal library, by design (ruling 2, DECISIONS.md 2026-09-02: "a personal
library is not a provenance"). Probed directly against the local Zotero 10
client on this host (port 23119, `Zotero is running`, confirmed live): the
account belongs to exactly one group, id `305258`, "ASEAN research
collaborative on environment and development", 13 560 real items — a live
shared research library, not a fixture target. `curl .../api/users/0/groups`
returns only that one row. Nothing here is a dedicated fixture group.

Zotero has no group-creation API. Verified independently (web search against
zotero.org's own API docs and forum threads, not taken on the earlier note's
word): group creation is zotero.org-website-only; the API only reads/writes
*inside* an existing group. A further check settles the group's required
*type*: DECISIONS.md's 2026-09-02 ruling 6 already says "a group-library slice
needs a closed group, since public open groups cannot hold files" for the
tally's separate group-library-slice dimension (child 3's scope, not this
one) — and an independent web search confirms the underlying Zotero
constraint generalizes: "Public, Open Membership" groups cannot have File
Editing enabled at all (neither stored nor linked attachments), only
"Private" or "Public, Closed Membership" groups can. Since this child's
corpus injection also writes linked-file attachments, the *same* constraint
applies to the primary corpus's library, not only to the group-library-slice
dimension — a detail the ticket 0029 body's "public Zotero library" wording
does not spell out.

## What is proven versus what is exercised only on invented data

`bench/fixtures/golden_fixture.py` (876 lines) and
`bench/fixtures/make_index_fixture.mjs`'s `loadGoldenExport`/
`goldenReplayResponse` (906 lines total) are written generically: both loop
over an arbitrary-length recipe array (`for doc in recipe`, `recipe.flatMap`,
`recipeById.size` bijection checks against the manifest), so nothing in the
code is hardcoded to one document, one language, or one archive shape.
Verified by reading both files in full.

`tests/test_golden_fixture_harness.py` (1210 lines, 79 passed / 1 skipped,
re-run clean at HEAD here) is honest about its own scope in its module
docstring: "The tests use invented one-item API responses. They prove the
machinery without pretending those responses are ticket 0029's still-
unavailable live export." Verified directly: every test recipe in the file
(`recipe_for`, `representative_recipe`) is English, `internet-archive`, and
at most one parent document with at most two attachments (a PDF/HTML pair
exercising `test_representative_parent_reconciles_multiple_attachments_
independently` and `test_representative_export_binds_two_attachments_and_
their_semantics`). No test recipe has more than one top-level parent item,
none uses Gallica/HAL/Wikisource/FAOLEX/Wikimedia-Commons archive shapes,
`djvu`/`epub`/`wikitext` bytes formats, or a non-English `language` field. So
the *mechanism* for multi-document, multi-language, mixed-attachment-format
injection is written and structurally sound by inspection, but has never been
*exercised* against the real 17-document, 4-language (en/fr/vi/de),
5-archive-type shape of `bench/fixtures/recipe.json`. That gap can only close
with a real injection + export run — this ticket's blocked half.

## What this ticket did without a live public group

- Re-verified `pytest tests/test_fixture_recipe.py tests/test_golden_fixture_
  harness.py -q`: 79 passed, 1 skipped (matches PR #294's own verification).
- Confirmed `bench/fixtures/recipe.json`'s live state: 26 records, 17 hashed,
  9 open (`cournot-1838-recherches`, `malynes-1622-lex-mercatoria`,
  `depitre-1908-oeuvres-cournot`, `ha-duong-2005-modeles-de-precaution-hdr`,
  `ha-duong-1998-irreversibilite-these`, `hal-04332519-economies-of-scale`,
  `hal-04826774-lich-su-sach-nam-ky`, `des-michels-1883-luc-van-tien`,
  `des-michels-1884-kim-van-kieu-t2p1`) — matches `bench/fixtures/README.md`'s
  own table.
- Read `bench/fixtures/golden_fixture.py` and the replay half of
  `bench/fixtures/make_index_fixture.mjs` in full against the real recipe
  shape (see above): no defect found; the residual risk is untested breadth,
  not a code bug.
- Pinned the `index_fulltext_max_chars` discrepancy the 2026-09-02/03
  scoping brief flagged (0029 log, 22:41Z entry) and traced it to source:
  `SPEC.md:1008`, `DEFAULT_FULLTEXT_MAX_CHARS = 40_000` at
  `fulltext-source.ts:11`, is zoteus's own shipped cap on how much of
  Zotero's `/fulltext` response it indexes per item — separate from Zotero's
  own extraction limits (100 pages / 500 000 characters, SPEC.md:2455,
  `fulltext.pdfMaxPages`/`fulltext.textMaxLength`). `bench/run_build.py:72`'s
  `--max-chars` CLI default is `"200000"`, a bench-harness convenience value
  five times larger, with no comment tying it to the shipped default.
  **Ruling for this export: `--index-max-chars 40000`, matching the shipped
  product default**, not `run_build.py`'s bench-convenience 200000 — a golden
  fixture is supposed to prove the harness against what a real install does,
  and 200000 would silently let five times more per-document content through
  the index than any user of the shipped extension gets, exactly the kind of
  per-axis silent-default drift this repo's own defect history warns about.
  If a future change moves the shipped default, this export's pin moves with
  it and is re-exported, not left stale.
- Staged, not yet run (needs the library from the open question below):

  ```
  ZOTEUS_LOCAL_API_KEY=<from a Zotero 10 local grant> \
  python3 bench/fixtures/golden_fixture.py \
    --library-type group --library-id <NEW_GROUP_ID> \
    --collection-key <NEW_COLLECTION_KEY> \
    inject --cache-dir <fetch_recipe.py's cache dir>

  ZOTEUS_LOCAL_API_KEY=<same> \
  python3 bench/fixtures/golden_fixture.py \
    --library-type group --library-id <NEW_GROUP_ID> \
    --collection-key <NEW_COLLECTION_KEY> \
    export --cache-dir <same> \
    --destination bench/fixtures/export \
    --zotero-client-version "<read from Help > About Zotero at run time>" \
    --pdf-max-pages 100 --text-max-length 500000 \
    --index-max-chars 40000
  ```

  `--pdf-max-pages 100`/`--text-max-length 500000` are Zotero's documented
  stock defaults (SPEC.md:2455); confirm they still read that way in the
  injecting client's Settings > Advanced before running, since the tool
  requires them as explicit input specifically so a customized profile can't
  silently masquerade as the stock one. `fetch_recipe.py`'s cache directory
  and the client version string are read at run time, not guessed here.

## Live state after the real injection

The group, plugin, and attachment-storage questions described below were real
and are now resolved (author, 2026-09-04) and independently re-verified: group
6659303, collection 3AY48MA5, `ZOTEUS_LOCAL_API_KEY`, and
`bench/zotero-fulltext-plugin` all confirmed live; group items use uploaded
`imported_file` attachments against the author's paid Zotero storage plan.
The injection completed for all 17 records.

The export boundary is now code (log, 2026-09-06). The three failure-control
attachments — the two Vietnamese volumes (DjVu and an un-OCR'd scan) and
Ramsey's un-OCR'd scan, all three ruled to stay (author, 2026-09-04 and
2026-09-06) — are declared as `failure_control` on their recipe records, and
`_snapshot_rows` accepts an attachment without full text only on the settled
state the reindex of the same run observed for it, never on mere absence from
the `/fulltext` census. The disappearance check therefore stands, and a new
guard refuses an indexed attachment whose fulltext version the reindex left
unchanged (no file read on this client).

What remains is the run itself, and it is bound to one machine: the injecting
client is padme's Zotero (fresh data dir `~/data/Zotero-fresh`, the local key,
the plugin, all 17 files), which was not running on 2026-09-06 and has no
graphical session or Xvfb to start it from. doudou holds the group by sync
only — no files, synced full text — and an export there would be refused by
the new guard, correctly. The verified cache now lives at
`~/data/golden-fixture-cache` on both machines (17 `match`). The exact
command, expected shape and replay step are in the 2026-09-06 log. The
RDF-metadata plus full-text-capture split the author proposed is not started;
it is a possible redesign to weigh once this export exists.

---

Ticket 0029's body says the corpus goes into "a collection of a public Zotero
library," and this repo's only reachable Zotero account belongs to exactly
one group (305258, the live ASEAN research library) — not a fixture target,
and never to be touched by this tool. Zotero groups cannot be created via
API (verified above), so this is squarely one decision for the author, not a
default to invent:

**Please create a new, dedicated Zotero group for ticket 0029's golden-
fixture corpus, separate from group 305258.** Per DECISIONS.md's own ruling
("public open groups cannot hold files") and the independent confirmation
above, it must be **"Public, Closed Membership"** (not "Public, Open
Membership" — that type cannot have File Editing enabled at all, so the
linked-file attachments this harness writes would be rejected; not "Private"
either, since the ticket's own ruling calls for a *public* library). Once it
exists: share its numeric group id, and grant local-API write access to
whichever Zotero 10 desktop client will run the injection (the client must
join the group, then issue a `ZOTEUS_LOCAL_API_KEY` local grant for it —
see `bench/fixtures/golden_fixture.py`'s `_client()`/`ZoteroLocalClient`).
A name/description is the author's call; "zoteus golden fixture (ticket
0029)" or similar is a reasonable default if none is specified.

This was the original group-creation request. It no longer blocks: the author
created group 6659303, granted the local write key, installed the control
plugin, selected stored attachments, and the 17-record injection completed.

## Relevant files
- `bench/fixtures/golden_fixture.py` — injection/export CLI (PR #294, pre-
  existing, re-verified here)
- `bench/fixtures/make_index_fixture.mjs` — `loadGoldenExport`/
  `goldenReplayResponse`, the Zotero-free replay side (PR #294, pre-existing,
  re-verified here)
- `bench/fixtures/recipe.json`, `bench/fixtures/README.md` — the source
  recipe and its documentation (26 records, 17 hashed)
- `bench/fixtures/fetch_recipe.py` — re-fetches and verifies source bytes
  against the recipe's pinned hashes
- `bench/golden_gate.py` — downstream consumer, deliberately agnostic to how
  its input JSON was produced (out of this ticket's scope; consumes whatever
  export eventually lands)
- `bench/run_build.py:72` — the `--max-chars` default this ticket found
  inconsistent with the shipped product default; not changed here (that
  default serves other bench call sites too; changing it is a separate call)
- `tests/test_golden_fixture_harness.py` — proves the machinery on invented
  one-item data; does not exercise the real multi-document/multi-language
  shape (see "What is proven" above)
- `SPEC.md:1008`, `SPEC.md:2455` — the two extraction-cap citations this
  ticket traced and pinned

